>>
Rule 1 (input must be a tensor to avoid TypeError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input dtype must be floating to avoid "elu_cpu" not implemented for 'Char')
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 3 (alpha must be non-zero to avoid ZeroDivisionError)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 4 (inplace must be a boolean)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = true ∨ v_1 = false
>>
Rule 5 (in-place CELU only valid for floating-point input dtype)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= (v_1 = false) ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
